    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      Let $K$ be a $\kappa $-small simplicial set, and $\overline{p}: K^{\triangleright } \rightarrow \calC $ a colimit diagram. We wish to show that $j \circ \overline{p}: K^{\triangleright } \rightarrow \Ind _{\kappa }(\calC )$ is also a colimit diagram. Let $C \in \Ind _{\kappa }(\calC )$ be an object, and let $F: \Ind _{\kappa }(\calC )^{op} \rightarrow \hat{\SSet }$ be the functor represented by $F$. According to Proposition <a href="/tag/1F6842" data-tag="1F6842">5.1.3.2</a>, it will suffice to show that $F \circ (j \circ \overline{p})^{op}$ is a limit diagram in $\SSet $. We observe that $F \circ j^{op}$ is equivalent to the object $C \in \Ind _{\kappa }(\calC ) \subseteq \Fun ( \calC ^{op}, \SSet )$, and therefore $\kappa $-right exact. We now conclude by invoking Proposition <a href="/tag/E3BF32" data-tag="E3BF32">5.3.2.9</a>. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>